# Episode 2: The Coffee Cup

Detective D. Torque arrived at the scene before sunrise.

A wealthy businessman had been found dead in his office. Police believed it was a heart attack.

Everyone was ready to close the case.

But D. Torque noticed a half-finished cup of coffee sitting on the desk.

The cup had lipstick on the rim.

The victim lived alone.

Something didn't fit.

Torque sent the coffee for testing.

The results revealed traces of a rare poison.

The poison had been added after the coffee was prepared.

Security footage showed a woman entering the building shortly before the victim died.

When questioned, she claimed she had never entered the office.

Torque showed her the footage.

She confessed.

The victim had discovered her embezzling money from the company.

Afraid of being exposed, she poisoned his drink.

The death was ruled a homicide.

Case Closed.

But before leaving, Torque found a strange symbol drawn inside the victim's desk drawer.

The same symbol from Case #1.

Someone was connecting the crimes.
